.TH DWM 1 "dwm-VERSION" "dwm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwm \- dynamic window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dwm
is a dynamic window manager for X. It manages windows in tiled, monocle and
floating layouts. Layouts can be applied dynamically, optimizing the
environment for the application in use and the task performed.
.PP
.B dwm
does not offer any graphical configuration; customization is done by editing
config.h and recompiling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information to standard output and exit.
.SH USAGE
When
.B dwm
starts, the first workspace is selected. Every new window is assigned to the
current workspace. Windows can be moved between workspaces with the keyboard
and are tiled according to the active layout.
.PP
The status bar at the top of the screen displays workspace names, the current
layout symbol and the root window name, which can be updated with
.BR xsetroot (1).
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
.B dwm
is customized by editing
.I config.h
and running
.BR "make clean install" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.h
Configuration header, symlinked to
.IR include/config.h .
.SH BUGS
Please report bugs to the dwm mailing list or the project's issue tracker.
.SH AUTHOR
dwm was written by Anselm R. Garbe and contributors.
